se lines: `<TIMESTAMP> | account_service | <RESOURCE_ID> | USER_PROFILE | NOT_FOUND | <EMAIL>`\r\n   - Insert into `evidence_records`: `(file_id='evidence_03', captured_at, 'account_service', resource_id, 'ABSENT', user_id=None, email=email)`.\r\n\r\n4. LINK PRIMARY ACCOUNTS FROM `system_activity`:\r\n   - Match deletion requests to `system_activity` where:\r\n     `details LIKE 'Deletion worker submitted primary profile account_% to account_service.'`\r\n   - Match by event window: `event_time` is between `requested_at` and `reported_at` (or within 10 minutes prior to `reported_at`).\r\n   - If multiple candidates exist, pick the one closest to `reported_at`.\r\n   - Map that `account_XXXX` as the primary account for that user/request in `evidence_records` with:\r\n     `system_id='account_service'`, `resource_id=account_id`, `verified_state='ABSENT'`, `user_id=req_user_id`, `email=req_email`.\r\n\r\n======================================================================\r\nPART 2: UPDATE `src/pipeline.py` (`audit_case` and `build_steps_json`)\r\n======================================================================\r\n\r\n1. TOPOLOGICAL SYSTEM PRECEDENCE ORDER:\r\n   In the `VERIFICATION` phase, steps must strictly follow this order:\r\n   SYSTEM_ORDER = {\r\n       \"account_service\": 1,\r\n       \"search_service\": 2,\r\n       \"security_service\": 3,\r\n       \"support_platform\": 4,\r\n       \"identity_service\": 5,\r\n       \"analytics_platform\": 6,\r\n       \"integration_service\": 7,\r\n       \"backup_service\": 8,\r\n       \"export_service\": 9\r\n   }\r\n   Sort key for verification steps: (SYSTEM_ORDER.get(step[\"system_id\"], 99), step[\"resource_id\"]).\r\n\r\n2. COMPLIANCE RULE FOR AUDIT RECORDS (rule_12):\r\n   - `security_service` audit records are legally required retention records.\r\n   - NEVER generate `REPORT_REMAINING_RECORD` or `DELETE_RECORD` for `security_service`.\r\n   - If an `audit_record_*` exists for the user, verify it under